# The owner keeps a stranded or skipped value: it does not take a write made
# before the switch into its resolution of the contested key, as 10.2.0's origin
# does while the old leaf strands it, so a write stamped later than the bulk entry
# loses on the origin and wins on every replica and view. Moved from the design;
# it edits the owner's resolution, so it names no perturbed action.
MODULE: ContestedKeyAgreesStrandedValueKept
TARGET: ContestedKeyAgrees
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the owner resolves a contested key without a later-stamped write made before the switch

--- FIND
OwnerRank == Top({o \in heldN : o <= rpN /\ author[o] # "s"})
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: writes made before the switch are not part of the owner's resolution.
OwnerRank == Top({o \in heldN : o <= rpN /\ author[o] \notin {"p", "c", "s"}})
--- END
